// Q-093 `date.valid` passes a date-time that the date functions then refuse with a runtime error (a 500, not an error value), and a record cannot say a field is a date: text from a page checked with `date.valid` still ends a request
// mode: serve
// get: /next?d=2026-11-20
// get: /next?d=2026-11-20T08:00:00Z
// open-when: 500
// open-when: /`date.valid`.*(argument|expects)/
// fixed-when: T08:00:00Z -> 400
// From FEEDBACK13.md §Q-093 (found on add81dc). Fixed by `date.valid(s, "date")`, which takes only a date.

route GET /next ? { d: str } = date.valid(d, "date") ? date.add_days(d, 1) : respond(400, "not a date")
